<title>BELGIUM: Belgian BASF Antwerp 1996 net profit falls by 1/3.</title>
<headline>Belgian BASF Antwerp 1996 net profit falls by 1/3.</headline>
<dateline>ANTWERP, Belgium 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31,</p>
<p>1996 (figures in millions of Belgian francs)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   4,290    vs    6,733</p>
<p>    Operating profit   7,382    vs   10,683</p>
<p>    Sales		 75,013    vs   72,419</p>
<p>    Cash flow	   16,066    vs   17,659</p>
<p>    Workforce	    3,608    vs    3,597</p>
<p>NOTE - BASF Antwerpen NV is the German chemicals group BASF's largest European production unit. It expects 1997 investments of between five and six billion Belgian francs after 8.2 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>BASF Antwerpen said results were affected by weak demand, low stock levels and rising raw materials prices.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
